1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:06,173
In Vṛndāvana the cowherds kept a festival for Indra, lord of rain.

2
00:00:06,173 --> 00:00:14,120
But young Kṛṣṇa watched the cattle graze the green slopes of Govardhana, and wondered why the mountain that fed them went unthanked.

3
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:21,968
"Worship what feeds you," said Kṛṣṇa. "These pastures, these cows, this hill —

4
00:00:21,968 --> 00:00:27,871
they give us all we have. Honour Govardhana, and let the pride of distant Indra go.

5
00:00:27,871 --> 00:00:30,431
" And the herders, trusting, agreed.

6
00:00:32,731 --> 00:00:38,192
Robbed of his worship, Indra raged. He loosed the clouds of doomsday upon Vṛndāvana —

7
00:00:38,192 --> 00:00:45,002
seven nights of blinding rain, thunder without mercy, to drown the herders and their impudent cowherd boy.

8
00:00:47,802 --> 00:00:52,911
Then Kṛṣṇa reached down, and lifted Govardhana whole upon his little finger.

9
00:00:52,911 --> 00:00:56,003
The mountain rose like a vast green umbrella —

10
00:00:56,003 --> 00:01:00,708
and all Vṛndāvana, herder and cow and calf, sheltered beneath it, dry.

11
00:01:05,108 --> 00:01:08,931
Seven days and seven nights the rain hammered the world.

12
00:01:08,931 --> 00:01:11,730
Yet under the mountain not one drop fell.

13
00:01:11,730 --> 00:01:18,078
Kṛṣṇa held it steady, smiling, while the storm spent its fury on the unbroken circle of calm.

14
00:01:21,478 --> 00:01:25,023
At last Indra's storm broke, and shamed, he bowed.

15
00:01:25,023 --> 00:01:30,765
The sun returned to a washed and shining Vṛndāvana. Kṛṣṇa set the mountain down —

16
00:01:30,765 --> 00:01:34,451
and the cowherds hailed him Govinda, keeper of cows.
